{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 08:42:50 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: manage_docs_testing_playground] Investigated read_file search behavior in sentinel mode: rehydrated via query_entries (global) and inspected tools/read_file.py + docs/Scribe_Usage.md; search_mode defaults to literal, regex runs line-by-line, and regex inference only flips to smart when query is used. This likely explains regex misses for cross-line patterns (e.g., progress_log.*parent). Next: implement multiline regex fallback and make smart/regex the default for search. | priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/manage_docs_testing_playground/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T08:42:50.102500+00:00_aaf1f160", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T08:42:50.102533+00:00"}
